WEB SOURCE (the specification)
  web/src/features/driving/components/drivetrain-health/HealthGaugeGrid.tsx — a presentational leaf fed
  { overallHealth, healthScore, motorStatus, sensors, stats? } by the Drivetrain Health page, plus useUnits()
  (unitPrefs.distance ∈ {km,mi,ft}; unitPrefs.speed ∈ {km/h,mph}). It renders a responsive Grid(cols 1 / md 3):
    Panel 1  RadialGauge(value=healthScore, max=100, unit="%", color=HEALTH_COLOR[overallHealth], size=140)
             + <p> "Overall drivetrain condition rating".
    Panel 2  "Motor Details" KVList: Motor Status=motorStatus · Overall Health=capitalize(overallHealth) ·
             Health Score=`${healthScore}%` · Active Sensors=String(sensors.filter(s=>s.value!==null).length);
             footer Activity icon + "Real-time telemetry active".
    Panel 3  "Drive Statistics": stats ? KVList[ Total Drives=fmtInt(totalDrives) ·
             Total Distance=`${fmtInt(convertDistanceFromSI(totalDistanceKm))} ${distanceUnit}` ·
             Avg Speed=`${fmtNumber(convertSpeedFromSI(avgSpeedKmh),1)} ${speedUnit}` ·
             Top Speed=`${fmtNumber(convertSpeedFromSI(topSpeedKmh),1)} ${speedUnit}` ] : <Skeleton lines={4} />.
  Data hooks: useTranslation, useUnits. The parent owns loading/error; the inner stats===undefined branch is a
  per-panel skeleton. HEALTH_COLOR: good #10b981 · warning #f59e0b · critical #ef4444.

